==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|chasse}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|chassé}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|dance}} A [[gliding]] [[movement]] in [[dance]] (especially [[ballet]]) with the same [[foot]] always [[leading]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|past2=~d}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To perform this step.
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[dismiss]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1817|title=The Literary Gazette
|passage=We believe that this sans-culotte Pillet or Pillard, Pendard or Fuyard, was so put to his shifts that the want of both might have '''chasséd''' him from decent society.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1868|author=Percy Fitzgerald|title=The Life of David Garrick|page=32
|passage=Garrick soon found out this double dealing, and '''''chasséd''''' him promptly.}}

